Apache-2.0 is one-way compatible with AGPL-3.0, so the AGPL crates may depend on
mm-model and mm-markdown. The reverse is not true: neither Apache-2.0 crate may
ever take code, or a dependency, from an AGPL-licensed crate or from
server/channels/. That constraint is the same one the existing dependency rule
already enforces — mm-model and mm-markdown have zero internal dependencies —
but it is now a licensing requirement and not only an architectural one.

The four AGPL crates are still stubs at the time of writing. They carry
AGPL-3.0-only ahead of holding any AGPL-derived line, deliberately: the label is
a precondition for the first such commit, not a consequence of it.


MODIFICATIONS
-------------

Apache License 2.0, section 4(b) requires derivative works to carry prominent
notices stating that files have been changed. They have been, extensively, and
the same is true of the AGPL-licensed portion:

This project is a **translation** of Mattermost server source from Go to Rust.
Apart from webapp/ (below), no file here is a copy of an upstream file. Every
Rust module is a reimplementation of the corresponding Go source, restructured
for Rust's type system, and in a small number of documented cases it deliberately behaves
differently from the original. Those divergences are enumerated in
`docs/TECH_DEBT.md`; the per-file semantics are recorded in `MIGRATION.md`.

Rust source files cite their Go origin in a doc comment, for example:

    //! Port of `server/public/model/channel.go`.

Files under `fixtures/` are generated by running the upstream Go code and
recording its output; they contain no upstream source.

The webapp
----------

`webapp/` is the one exception to "no file here is a copy". It is upstream's
browser client, copied unmodified from the pinned commit above so the stack can
be driven from a browser. Its files keep their upstream copyright headers and
remain under the Apache License v2.0, as granted by upstream's LICENSE.txt
(quoted above); the full text is upstream's server/public/LICENSE.txt, of which
crates/mm-model/LICENSE is a byte-identical copy. Any future change to a file
under webapp/ must be recorded here, as section 4(b) requires.


